The `(fn [inner] ...)` interp closure is passed to `free-run` as a `^fat`
tur_poly_fn_t and never dropped by the caller -- the deferred
escaping-fat-closure-env leak (docs/reported/escaping-fat-closure-env-leak.md).
The leak is present in the emitted C on BOTH the direct and the (now) CPS path;
the direct-emitter `int main` merely hid it from LeakSanitizer via stack
reachability. Once the closure carries RC/drop glue this marker can be removed.
